 "notes": "The Virginia Employment Commission's Report to Determine Liability. Most boxes are character cells: names and addresses are cut at the cell count (30 for names and streets), phones print area code, exchange and number in their own cells, ZIP codes as five digits and the plus-four, dates as month, day and year. The FEIN prints as 2 and 7 digits. Answers 'No' or 'Yes: MM/DD/YYYY' for the FUTA and liability questions tick the box and write the date. The locality is the city or county where the work is done; an answer naming a county ticks County, otherwise City. The responsible party's SSN cells are never printed; the signer writes them. Only the general-employer liability questions are asked; the agricultural, domestic and nonprofit questions, the acquisition details and the signature date are left for the signer.",
